{"adjusted_volatile_messages": [["user","Prepare the requested reusable draft without executing any operation."]], "bridge_messages": [], "composition_summary": "Drafted one unapproved pure-logic class-22 component for the records list validator. Raw records is a required list of 1..3 items; each item has exactly code (string length 2..5) and enabled (exact bool, False valid). Missing/null/wrong types/extra fields are invalid without exceptions or coercion. The helper receives the whole mapping to distinguish absent from explicit null; module code calls it and assigns result. No I/O, imports, host calls, upstream validation assumption, tests or approval claims. No execution, submission, Q1/Q2 or activation was performed by this example reviewer.", "proposed_components": [{"class_code": 22, "payload": {"name": "pc-contrast-07", "description": "Raw records must be a list of 1..3 items. Every object has exactly code and enabled. code is a string of length 2..5 inclusive. enabled is an exact bool (False valid). Always result={ok:boolean, records:original if valid else []}. Empty is invalid; missing/null/wrong types/extra fields invalid without exceptions/coercion. No I/O/imports/host calls, no upstream validation assumption. Preserve conversation; target-input unapproved draft only, no tests or approval claims.", "content": "def validate_records(mapping):
    records = mapping.get('records')
    valid = type(records) is list and 1 <= len(records) <= 3
    if valid:
        for item in records:
            if type(item) is not dict or set(item) != {'code', 'enabled'}:
                valid = False
                break
            if not (type(item['code']) is str and 2 <= len(item['code']) <= 5 and type(item['enabled']) is bool):
                valid = False
                break
    result = {'ok': valid, 'records': records if valid else []}"}}], "proposed_intent_examples": [], "proposed_recipe_updates": [], "settings_adjustments": []}
